<h2 id="nashville-micro-markets">Nashville's side hustle micro-markets</h2>
<p>Each part of the metro creates a different kind of demand. Know which one you're working:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Downtown, SoBro and The Gulch:</strong> tourists, bachelorette groups, conventions and stadium crowds. Best for rideshare, event staffing and rental cleaning.</li>
  <li><strong>East Nashville, Germantown and 12 South:</strong> younger professionals in condos and renovated bungalows. Great for delivery, dog walking and short-term rental work.</li>
  <li><strong>Franklin, Brentwood and Green Hills:</strong> high household incomes and big yards. Ideal for lawn care, pressure washing, tutoring, cleaning and pet sitting.</li>
  <li><strong>Midtown and West End:</strong> Vanderbilt and Belmont students plus Music Row. Best for tutoring, moving help and creative gigs.</li>
  <li><strong>Murfreesboro, Mt. Juliet and Hendersonville:</strong> fast-growing suburbs with new construction, which means furniture assembly, handyman and moving work.</li>
</ul>

